    <briefdescription>
<para>Reduce-by-segment functor. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given two cub::KeyValuePair inputs <computeroutput>a</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>b</computeroutput> and a binary associative combining operator <computeroutput>f(const T &amp;x, const T &amp;y)</computeroutput>, an instance of this functor returns a cub::KeyValuePair whose <computeroutput>key</computeroutput> field is <computeroutput>a.key + b.key</computeroutput>, and whose <computeroutput>value</computeroutput> field is either <computeroutput>b.value</computeroutput> if <computeroutput>b.key</computeroutput> is non-zero, or <computeroutput>f(a.value, b.value)</computeroutput> otherwise.</para>
<para><ref refid="structcub_1_1ReduceBySegmentOp" kindref="compound">ReduceBySegmentOp</ref> is an associative, non-commutative binary combining operator for input sequences of cub::KeyValuePair pairings. Such sequences are typically used to represent a segmented set of values to be reduced and a corresponding set of {0,1}-valued integer &quot;head flags&quot; demarcating the first value of each segment.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ReductionOpT</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Binary reduction operator to apply to values </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
